WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.210
SPEAKER: When everybody
first discovers Kubernetes,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.290
it feels like an
end unto itself,

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.265
where you could do so many
things with Kubernetes.

00:00:11.265 --> 00:00:13.390
And as you become more
comfortable with Kubernetes,

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:14.765
what you realize
is it's actually

00:00:14.765 --> 00:00:17.290
just a stepping stone to
so many other solutions

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.910
and possibilities.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.730
You look at the power behind
it, a solution like Anthos,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.800
for example, it
really encapsulates

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.720
all of Google's
learnings at scale

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.450
to how we help
customers experience

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.690
the same benefits and
value and all of the things

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.040
that the cloud-native
landscape has to offer,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.820
but in a way that is
explicitly curated by Google's

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.080
expertise in the space.

00:00:43.222 --> 00:00:45.680
Kubernetes is the level playing
field for all those things.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.780
It's essentially a
platform that empowers

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.040
infinite possibilities.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

